{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1349395-healing-orchid","id":1349395,"title":"Healing Orchid","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-11-18T12:10:35-08:00","id":1349395,"title":"Healing Orchid","content":"I was thinking of doing a sorcerous working to try to make an orchid into an 2nd Edition Healing orchid. What do you think the level would be?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10745-nosleeves","name":"nosleeves","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-18T13:03:52-08:00","id":1349421,"title":"","content":"What were the effects of the Healing Orchid? I don't recall them offhand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-18T13:42:34-08:00","id":1349434,"title":"","content":"Commit 3m<br /> Heal 1 lvl B/hour<br /> Heal 1 lvl L/ 3hours<br /> bonus to poison","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10745-nosleeves","name":"nosleeves","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-18T13:48:36-08:00","id":1349437,"title":"","content":"If it's a lasting object that you can just carry around and give to other people, I'd say that's an Artifact. <br /> <br /> More importantly, <i>why</i> does this character want a Healing Orchid? What's their intent and desired end result? <br /> Are they trying to replace Danny Dawn's lost arm (again)? <br /> Are they trying to make sure Danny Dawn stops nearly dying so often by giving him super-healing? <br /> Are they trying to show off their mastery of sorcery by creating a mythical plant? <br /> Because &quot;Healing Orchid&quot; may or may not just be a step on the way to their real end result, and that's critically important for Workings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-18T13:54:06-08:00","id":1349439,"title":"","content":"I am looking to start a species of plant that grows in a particular manse. Also maybe to decrease down time due to healing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10745-nosleeves","name":"nosleeves","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-18T14:06:21-08:00","id":1349442,"title":"","content":"1st Edition. Ruins of Rathes.<br /> <br /> Like Scavenger Son's healing flowers which they are an upgrade of, I'm pretty sure they don't appear in 2E.<br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure I'd handle it as an Artifact.<br /> <br /> But it's bestowing a power, Celestial 2. Power is transferable, Celestial 3. Really, it's three powers, Solar 1. And you want it growing new copies in your manse, Solar 2. You specifically want it as a flower? Finesse 5.<br /> <br /> (If you just want to give one mortal Exalted Healing, that's Celestial 2 and the flower is a neat little side effect.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 11-18-2019, 05:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-18T14:12:07-08:00","id":1349446,"title":"","content":"2nd Ed They appear in the Debris of Fallen Races","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10745-nosleeves","name":"nosleeves","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-18T23:38:21-08:00","id":1349506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nosleeves</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1349395-healing-orchid?p=1349446#post1349446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2nd Ed They appear in the Debris of Fallen Races</div> </div> </div> </div>My mistake.<br /> <br /> Sorry about that.<br /> <br /> Debris slipped my mind <i>for some reason</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T07:48:30-08:00","id":1349587,"title":"","content":"If the orchid really grows in only a single manse, and can't grow <i>anywhere</i> else, I'd be okay with that as a Celestial 3 working. If it can grow in any manse or demesne, that would bump it up to Solar 1 for me. I wouldn't allow a given orchid to work indefinitely in any case, though - a self-reproducing thing that can give healing indefinitely is just too powerful for the setting. I'd say that it's like any cut flower - you can preserve it for a while, perhaps up to a week or a bit more, but once it withers, that's it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"",